      "retention_rule": "none",
      "deletion_mechanism": "tenant-purge.service.ts POSTs /purge to idFromName(tenantId)",
      "export_mechanism": "none",
      "tenant_scope": "per-tenant",
      "evidence_level": "E2",
      "note": "Persists a `state` key on every mutation (seven ctx.storage.put sites), so unlike its per-inspection sibling this one has an explicit object at rest. Addressed by idFromName(tenantId), so it needs no pre-cascade collection to be reachable."
    },
    {
      "store_type": "durable_object",
      "binding": "INSPECTION_PRESENCE",
      "modes": ["standalone", "saas"],
      "role": {
        "EU":    { "legal_role": "processor",    "basis": "tos.json §5 — presence is generated on the tenant's instruction while their staff work", "determined_at": "2026-08-15", "source": "contract + review" },
        "US_CA": { "legal_role": "unclassified", "basis": null, "determined_at": null, "source": null },
        "US_CO": { "legal_role": "unclassified", "basis": null, "determined_at": null, "source": null },
        "CA":    { "legal_role": "unclassified", "basis": null, "determined_at": null, "source": null }
      },
      "lifecycle_owner": "engine",
      "data_categories": ["presence_only", "staff_identity"],
      "subjects": ["staff"],
      "purpose": "Who is currently viewing one inspection, and which item each has focused.",
      "retention_rule": "connection-bounded",
      "deletion_mechanism": "none",
      "export_mechanism": "none",
      "tenant_scope": "not-tenant-scoped",
      "evidence_level": "E2",
      "note": "CORRECTED against the source. This class makes no ctx.storage call, but that does not make it stateless: it is a new_sqlite_classes Durable Object and its roster lives in WebSocket hibernation ATTACHMENTS (serializeAttachment), which the runtime persists so the object can sleep — the class comment says so itself. Each attachment carries userId, name and photoUrl. Two mitigations and one residual: the 90-second heartbeat sweep drops dead connections and an attachment cannot outlive its socket, so nothing accumulates; the residual is that it is addressed by idFromName(inspectionId) with NO tenant component, so a tenant purge has no way to enumerate these objects even once B1c gives them a purge verb."
    },
    {
      "store_type": "durable_object",
      "binding": "INSPECTOR_MCP",
      "modes": ["standalone", "saas"],
      "role": {
