        "US_CA": { "legal_role": "unclassified", "basis": null, "determined_at": null, "source": null },
        "US_CO": { "legal_role": "unclassified", "basis": null, "determined_at": null, "source": null },
        "CA":    { "legal_role": "unclassified", "basis": null, "determined_at": null, "source": null }
      },
      "lifecycle_owner": "vendor-library",
      "data_categories": ["mcp_session", "staff_identity"],
      "subjects": ["staff"],
      "purpose": "Remote MCP server session host — one object per authenticated MCP connection, carrying the caller's props (tenant and user identity).",
      "retention_rule": "unknown",
      "deletion_mechanism": "none",
      "export_mechanism": "none",
      "tenant_scope": "unknown",
      "evidence_level": "E2",
      "note": "The only entry whose lifecycle_owner is not us. Our subclass makes no ctx.storage call, but it extends McpAgent from the `agents` library and is declared new_sqlite_classes, so whatever that base class persists is at rest under our account and we did not write it. What it stores and how it is addressed are both UNKNOWN rather than none — reading the vendor's storage shape is the work that would let this entry make a claim."
    },

